[\n   \"ASM-1: When a signed decision supersedes an earlier decision, the service applies the new disposition to stock and order/route state and retains the prior decision; the web app displays the returned history and result.\",\n   \"ASM-2: Reports use on-screen date-range filters and CSV export; no custom report builder is included.\",\n   \"ASM-3 and ASM-14: Quality-decision escalation uses email from fixed templates only, with no SMS or push.\",\n   \"ASM-4 and ASM-15: Recall notices, 24-hour reminders, daily summaries, and monthly reports use email from fixed templates only, with no SMS or push.\",\n   \"ASM-5 and ASM-17: The responsive web app supports the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox, including offline driver work and photo/signature capture.\",\n   \"ASM-6 and ASM-18: Main flows target WCAG 2.1 AA conformance.\",\n   \"ASM-7: The first-year scale assumption is up to 1,000 users and 100,000 records; the trace screen must expose the returned trace within one minute of the request.\",\n   \"ASM-8: Departure is blocked until every expected route box has been scanned and every wrong box has been removed or corrected.\",\n   \"ASM-9: Offline route changes preserve unsent work, require review and resolution of affected boxes, and preserve completed handovers.\",\n   \"ASM-10: An offline handover that conflicts with a recall is retained, flagged, and associated with a quality case when synchronized.\",\n   \"ASM-11: If browser location is denied or unavailable, handover remains possible and location is recorded as unavailable.\",\n   \"ASM-12: The existing logger and supplier gateway provide live temperature, alert, box association, and temperature-history data through an API or feed supplied by Meridian.\",\n   \"ASM-13: Signing identity confirmation uses the account's sign-in method.\",\n   \"ASM-16: The customer portal uses the time zone configured on the user's account.\"\n  ],\n  \"nfrs\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-1\",\n    \"metric\": \"At viewport widths of 320, 768, and 1024 CSS pixels, all page content remains operable without horizontal page scrolling, and interactive touch targets are at least 44 by 44 CSS pixels.\",\n    \"text\": \"Every web-app page shall use a responsive layout for phone, tablet, and desktop widths, with touch-sized controls on narrow screens.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-2\",\n    \"metric\": \"100% of audited main-flow screens pass applicable WCAG 2.1 AA automated checks, with zero unresolved manual WCAG 2.1 AA failures.\",\n    \"text\": \"The main web-app flows shall conform to WCAG 2.1 AA.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-3\",\n    \"metric\": \"All critical sign-in, route, offline queue, handover, recall, customer-portal, and report UI tests pass on the latest two versions of each of the four named browsers.\",\n    \"text\": \"The responsive web app shall support the latest two browser versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-4\",\n    \"metric\": \"With fixtures representing 1,000 users and 100,000 records, the trace screen displays the complete returned trace within 60 seconds of the user's request.\",\n    \"text\": \"The web client shall support the assumed first-year product scale and make a requested lot trace available through its screen within the requested time limit.\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"outOfScope\": [\n   \"API-SIDE: Credential verification, password-reset delivery, account authorization, and enforcement of role, warehouse, and customer-organisation access scopes; the web requirements cover submitted requests and displayed service responses (Q-1, Q-2).\",\n   \"API-SIDE: Persisted state transitions and guarantees for stock holds, release/reject allocation changes, quarantine, destruction limits, route/order updates, recall accounting and closure, duplicate handover idempotency, and immutable signed decisions (ASM-1, Q-3, Q-6, Q-7).\",\n   \"API-SIDE: Enforcing seven-year retention of signatures, delivery photos, and audit records, and preventing or detecting alteration of persisted audit entries (Q-4).\",\n   \"API-SIDE: Scheduled and outbound email delivery, including four-hour quality escalation, customer recall notices and 24-hour reminders, daily warehouse summaries at 07:00, and first-of-month monthly reports; the web app presents available status and portal notices (ASM-3, ASM-4, ASM-14, ASM-15).\",\n   \"API-SIDE: Supplying live temperature readings, alert status, box associations, and temperature history through the existing logger or supplier gateway feed (ASM-12).\",\n   \"API-SIDE: Importing or guaranteeing the initial database contents, including the launch state of no imported records (Q-5); the web app provides opening-lot and stock entry.\",\n   \"Native iOS or Android applications, app-store distribution, push notifications, and background location; the product is a responsive web app, uses in-app notices or email where specified, requests location through the browser, and may be installable as a web app.\"\n  ],\n  \"requirements\": [\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A user is on the sign-in screen\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-1.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen sends a sign-in request containing the entered email and password and displays the returned sign-in result\",\n      \"when\": \"the user enters an email address and password and submits the form\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A user is on the sign-in screen\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-1.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen sends a password-reset request and displays the returned confirmation or error message\",\n      \"when\": \"the user opens password reset and submits an email address\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall provide individual email-and-password sign-in and a self-service password-reset flow for driver, staff, and customer areas.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-1\",\n    \"op\": 