the Meridian web app shall retain the handover and show the conflict and the returned quality-case status.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-11\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-14\",\n     \"I-16\",\n     \"I-41\",\n     \"I-46\",\n     \"I-47\",\n     \"ASM-10\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The service returns stop statuses and update times\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-12.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays each stop's returned status and last-updated time\",\n      \"when\": \"the dispatcher opens route monitoring\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When a dispatcher opens route monitoring, the Meridian web app shall show each stop's status and the time it was last updated.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-12\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-9\",\n     \"I-10\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The service returns an excursion's temperature history, tier budgets, and recommendation\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-13.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays the full returned history, used and remaining allowance per tier, and the recommendation\",\n      \"when\": \"a reviewer opens the excursion\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The configured tier limits and allowances are shown for two different products\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-13.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays the same configured tier limits and allowance values for both products\",\n      \"when\": \"a user views each product's excursion settings\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When an excursion is reviewed, the Meridian web app shall show the full temperature history, used and remaining allowance for each tier, and a recommendation based on one configured set of tier limits and allowances shared by all products.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-13\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-21\",\n     \"I-22\",\n     \"I-23\",\n     \"Q-8\",\n     \"ASM-12\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The excursion is confined to the first tier above or below the band and has allowance remaining\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-14.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen offers the single-officer decision workflow\",\n      \"when\": \"a Quality Officer opens the decision form\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The excursion is outside the single-officer case or has no allowance remaining\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-14.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen requires a proposal and a separate Quality Manager approval\",\n      \"when\": \"a Quality Officer opens the decision form\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The proposing Quality Officer also has the Quality Manager role\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-14.3\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen does not offer approval by that same person\",\n      \"when\": \"that person attempts to approve the proposal\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A proposed decision goes against the displayed recommendation\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-14.4\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen requires both decision participants and a written justification\",\n      \"when\": \"the user prepares the decision\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When a quality decision is prepared, the Meridian web app shall present the permitted decision workflow so that a Quality Officer may decide alone only for an excursion confined to the first tier above or below the band with allowance remaining, and all other decisions require a different Quality Manager approver.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-14\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-24\",\n     \"I-25\",\n     \"I-26\",\n     \"I-27\",\n     \"I-28\",\n     \"I-29\",\n     \"I-30\",\n     \"I-31\",\n     \"I-32\",\n     \"I-33\",\n     \"Q-6\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A user is submitting a quality decision\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-15.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen requires identity confirmation and a reason before sending the signing request\",\n      \"when\": \"the user signs the decision\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A decision is returned as signed\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-15.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows its signed values as read-only and provides a separate superseding-decision action\",\n      \"when\": \"a user opens that decision\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When a user signs a quality decision, the Meridian web app shall require identity confirmation using that account's sign-in method and a reason, and present a signed decision as read-only with a separate action to supersede it.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-15\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-25\",\n     \"I-33\",\n     \"I-34\",\n     \"I-35\",\n     \"ASM-13\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The service returns an earlier signed decision, its superseding decision, and resulting disposition\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-16.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays both decisions and the returned stock, order, and route disposition\",\n      \"when\": \"a user opens the affected handling unit\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A decision is signed as Release or Reject\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-16.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows released stock as available or restored to its order and route, or rejected stock as removed from its order\",\n      \"when\": \"the service returns the resulting disposition\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When a signed decision is superseded, the Meridian web app shall display both signed decisions and the returned resulting stock, order, and route disposition.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-16\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-34\",\n     \"I-35\",\n     \"I-36\",\n     \"ASM-1\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A user opens destruction entry for rejected stock\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-17.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the request contains the destruction date, quantity, and witness\",\n      \"when\": \"the user records destruction\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The entered destruction quantity exceeds the displayed rejected quantity\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-17.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows a validation error and sends no destruction request\",\n      \"when\": \"the user submits the destruction entry\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When rejected stock is recorded for destruction, the Meridian web app shall collect the destruction date, quantity, and witness and prevent entry of a quantity greater than the rejected quantity shown for that stock.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-17\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-36\",\n     \"I-37\",\n     \"I-38\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The service returns a decision waiting more than four hours as escalated\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-18.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen lists the decision and displays its escalated status\",\n      \"when\": \"a Quality Manager opens waiting decisions\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When a quality decision has been waiting for more than four hours, the Meridian web app shall identify it as escalated and show it in the Quality Manager's waiting-decisions view.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-18\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-37\",\n     \"I-38\",\n     \"ASM-3\",\n     \"ASM-14\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A Quality Manager opens recall start\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-19.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the recall request contains those values and the screen displays the returned recall result\",\n      \"when\": \"the manager enters the product, one or more lot numbers, reason, severity, and signature\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A user who is not a Quality Manager opens recall management\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-19.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen does not offer recall start or close actions\",\n      \"when\": \"the user views recall actions\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A Quality Manager closes a recall\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-19.3\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the close request contains the signature and the screen displays the returned close result or error\",\n      \"when\": \"the manager submits the signed close action\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"Where the user is a Quality Manager, the Meridian web app shall provide signed recall-start and recall-close flows, with recall start collecting a product, one or more lot numbers, a reason, and a severity.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-19\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-39\",\n     \"I-40\",\n     \"I-41\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The service returns recall trace rows for locations, boxes, routes, and customer deliveries\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-20.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays each returned location, box, route, delivery, and quantity\",\n      \"when\": \"a user opens the trace\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The service returns trace quantities and the lot's total received quantity\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-20.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays the returned trace total alongside the received quantity\",\n      \"when\": \"the user views the trace summary\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When a user opens a recall trace, the Meridian web app shall show returned quantities and locations for every affected warehouse location, box, route, and customer delivery.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-20\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-41\",\n     \"I-42\",\n     \"I-43\",\n     \"ASM-7\",\n     \"ASM-12\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The service returns a recall notice for the signed-in customer organisation\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-21.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays the recall notice and links it to the affected deliveries\",\n      \"when\": \"the customer opens the portal\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When a customer receives a recall notice, the Meridian web app shall show the notice in that customer's portal and provide a response entry point for the affected deliveries.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-21\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-41\",\n     \"I-44\",\n     \"ASM-4\",\n     \"ASM-15\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A customer opens a recall response for a delivery\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-22.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the response request contains the entered quantities for that delivery\",\n      \"when\": \"the customer enters on-hand, used or dispensed, and destroyed quantities\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The reported quantities total less than the quantity delivered\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-22.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen accepts the values and displays the difference as unaccounted\",\n      \"when\": \"the customer submits the response\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The reported quantities total more than the quantity delivered\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-22.3\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows a validation error and sends no response request\",\n      \"when\": \"the customer submits the response\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When a customer responds to a recall, the Meridian web app shall collect on-hand, used or dispensed, and destroyed pack quantities for each delivery, allow a total below the delivered quantity as unaccounted, and reject a total above the delivered quantity.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-22\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-41\",\n     \"I-45\",\n     \"I-46\",\n     \"Q-3\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The service returns recall progress and customers who have not responded\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-23.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays the accounted-pack percentage and the outstanding customer list\",\n      \"when\": \"a Quality Manager opens the recall\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A Quality Manager writes off an unaccounted quantity\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-23.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the request contains the signed justification\",\n      \"when\": \"the manager submits the write-off\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A recall has an unaccounted quantity with no signed write-off\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-23.3\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen blocks submission and displays the outstanding quantity\",\n      \"when\": \"a Quality Manager opens the close action\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When a recall is viewed or closed, the Meridian web app shall show the accounted-pack percentage and outstanding customers and require a Quality Manager's signed justification to submit a write-off of unaccounted quantity.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-23\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-41\",\n     \"I-46\",\n     \"I-47\",\n     \"Q-3\",\n     \"Q-6\",\n     \"ASM-15\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The service returns orders and delivery data for the signed-in customer organisation\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-24.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays the returned current and past orders, lots, expiry dates, and road-delivery arrival and temperature status\",\n      \"when\": \"the customer opens the portal\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A road delivery has other customers on its route\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-24.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows no other customer's identity or delivery details\",\n      \"when\": \"the customer views that delivery\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When a customer user opens the portal, the Meridian web app shall show that user's organisation's current and past orders, allocated lots and expiry dates, and for deliveries on the road the planned arrival time and in-range or out-of-range temperature status without showing other customers on the route.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-24\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-48\",\n     \"I-49\",\n     \"I-50\",\n     \"Q-2\",\n     \"ASM-16\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A completed delivery has a returned certificate available\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-25.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the browser downloads a PDF file containing the listed delivery, handover, temperature, excursion, and decision fields\",\n      \"when\": \"the customer requests its certificate\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Late temperature readings produce a returned new certificate version\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-25.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen lists both the earlier and new version for download\",\n      \"when\": \"the customer opens certificate versions\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When a customer opens a completed delivery, the Meridian web app shall provide a PDF certificate showing products, lots, expiry dates, quantities, receiver, handover time, each box's temperature chart from sealing to handover, excursions, and their signed decisions.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-25\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-50\",\n     \"ASM-4\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The user's preference is Arabic\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-26.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen and certificate display Arabic right-to-left layout, including tables and charts\",\n      \"when\": \"the user opens the portal and a delivery certificate\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The user's account has a configured time zone\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-26.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the displayed value is in that configured time zone\",\n      \"when\": \"the user views a date or time in the portal\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When a user selects Arabic, the Meridian web app shall render the portal, tables, charts, and certificate right to left, and display dates and times in the user's configured time zone.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-26\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-13\",\n     \"I-15\",\n     \"I-17\",\n     \"I-18\",\n     \"I-19\",\n     \"I-20\",\n     \"I-50\",\n     \"ASM-16\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The service returns audit entries\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-27.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays each entry's actor, time, changed fields, old and new values, and supplied reason\",\n      \"when\": \"an Auditor opens the audit trail\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"An Auditor selects record, user, date-range, and action-type filters\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-27.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows the matching returned list and offers export of that filtered view\",\n      \"when\": \"the filters are applied\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A user opens a lot's history\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-27.3\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows returned lot events from receipt through delivery or destruction in time order\",\n      \"when\": \"the history is displayed\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When an Auditor opens the audit trail, the Meridian web app shall show returned audit entries with actor, time, changed fields, old and new values, and reason where supplied, and provide filters by record, user, date range, and action type and filtered-view export.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-27\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-13\",\n     \"I-15\",\n     \"I-17\",\n     \"I-18\",\n     \"I-19\",\n     \"I-20\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The service returns report figures for a selected date range and warehouse\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-28.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays every listed report measure and its returned value\",\n      \"when\": \"staff open the reports screen\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A staff member has access to specified warehouses\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-28.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen offers only those warehouses and displays the returned filtered figures\",\n      \"when\": \"the staff member filters reports\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A user selects a date range and warehouse filter\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-28.3\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the browser downloads a CSV file for the selected filters\",\n      \"when\": \"the user exports the report\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When staff view reports, the Meridian web app shall show excursion counts and rates by route, driver, vehicle, and shipper-box type; rejected and destroyed packs by product and cause; on-time and in-full delivery percentages; average excursion-to-decision time; stock within 60 days of expiry by product and warehouse; and open recalls with progress, with date-range and warehouse filters and export.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-28\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-50\",\n     \"ASM-2\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A staff user opens opening-inventory entry\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-29.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the request contains the entered lot and stock fields and the screen displays the returned result or error\",\n      \"when\": \"the user enters a lot and its opening stock details\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When staff enter opening inventory in the new system, the Meridian web app shall provide forms to enter opening lots and stock records.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-29\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-20\",\n     \"Q-5\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"suggestions\": []\n },\n {\n  \"draft\": \"d3\",\n  \"assumptions\": [\n   \"ASM-1: A superseding signed disposition is applied to stock and order/route state, with the earlier decision and resulting changes retained.\",\n   \"ASM-2: Reports use on-screen lists with filters and CSV export; there is no custom report builder.\",\n   \"ASM-3 and ASM-14: More-than-four-hour decision escalation is by email from fixed templates only; no SMS or push.\",\n   \"ASM-4 and ASM-15: Recall notices and 24-hour reminders are email-only from fixed templates; no SMS or push.\",\n   \"ASM-5: Driver route work is delivered as responsive web behavior, supporting the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox.\",\n   \"ASM-6 and ASM-18: Main flows target WCAG 2.1 AA.\",\n   \"ASM-7: The first-year scale assumption is up to 1,000 users and 100,000 records.\",\n   \"ASM-8: Departure is blocked until every expected box is scanned and each wrong box is removed or corrected.\",\n   \"ASM-9: Offline work is retained after a route change; the driver reviews and resolves affected boxes before continuing, and completed handovers are preserved.\",\n   \"ASM-10: A handover completed offline despite a recall is retained, flagged as a conflict, and associated with a quality case when synchronized.\",\n   \"ASM-11: Handover can be completed when browser location is unavailable, with location recorded as unavailable.\",\n   \"ASM-12: Live temperature, alert, box-association, and history data are supplied by an existing gateway API or feed.\",\n   \"ASM-13: A signer confirms identity using the sign-in method configured for that account.\",\n   \"ASM-16: The portal uses the time zone configured on the user's account.\",\n   \"ASM-17: The responsive web app supports the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox.\",\n   \"ASM-18: The main flows target WCAG 2.1 AA.\"\n  ],\n  \"nfrs\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-1\",\n    \"metric\": \"100% of pages render at 320, 768, and 1280 CSS-pixel viewport widths without horizontal page scrolling; touch targets on the 320-pixel layout are at least 44 by 44 CSS pixels.\",\n    \"text\": \"Every page shall adapt to phone, tablet, and desktop widths, with touch-sized controls on the narrow layout.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-2\",\n    \"metric\": \"8 browser/version combinations per device class: the latest 2 versions of each of 4 named browsers.\",\n    \"text\": \"The responsive web app shall support the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox on desktop and mobile browsers.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-3\",\n    \"metric\": \"100% of applicable WCAG 2.1 AA success criteria are met on the main flows.\",\n    \"text\": \"The main flows shall conform to WCAG 2.1 AA.\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"outOfScope\": [\n   \"API-SIDE: credential verification, password reset delivery, account and role persistence, and enforcement of warehouse and customer-organisation access scopes; the web app's screens and requests are specified above.\",\n   \"API-SIDE: persistence and enforcement of stock status, allocation and handover restrictions, recall trace completeness and arithmetic, decision authorization, destruction quantity limits, write-off rules, deduplication of repeated handover submissions, and audit immutability or tamper detection.\",\n   \"API-SIDE/JOB: seven-year evidence and audit retention, sending scheduled daily/monthly report emails, 4-hour decision escalation emails, customer recall notices and 24-hour reminder emails, and generating the scheduled monthly report.\",\n   \"API-SIDE: the existing logger and supplier gateway implementation and its feed; the web app consumes temperature, status, alert, and history data supplied through the gateway API/feed.\"\n  ],\n  \"requirements\": [\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A user has an account and is on the sign-in page\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-1.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows the signed-in area for that account\",\n      \"when\": \"the user submits valid email and password credentials\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A user is on the sign-in page\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-1.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows a request confirmation message\",\n      \"when\": \"the user submits a password-reset request\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall provide individual email-and-password sign-in and a self-service password-reset flow.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-1\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"Q-1\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A System Administrator is viewing user management\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-2.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows controls for account status, roles, warehouse access, and customer-organisation access\",\n      \"when\": \"the administrator opens an account record\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A System Administrator has entered account details and access scopes\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-2.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows the account status returned by the service\",\n      \"when\": \"the administrator submits the account form\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When a System Administrator opens user management, the Meridian web app shall provide controls to create and deactivate accounts and assign roles, warehouse access, and customer-organisation access.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-2\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"Q-2\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The route list contains routes assigned to multiple drivers\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-3.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows only that driver's routes and their stops in route order\",\n      \"when\": \"a signed-in driver opens today's routes\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When a driver opens today's routes, the Meridian web app shall show only that driver's assigned routes and each route's stops in route order.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-3\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"ASM-5\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A route has stops with status and update-time values\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-4.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows each stop's status and last-updated time\",\n      \"when\": \"a dispatcher opens route tracking\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When a dispatcher opens route tracking, the Meridian web app shall show each stop's status and the time that status was last updated.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-4\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"ASM-5\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A route has expected boxes and the driver scans its loading boxes\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-5.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows the wrong or missing box and shows departure as blocked\",\n      \"when\": \"a scanned box belongs to another route or an expected box is not scanned\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Every expected box is scanned and any wrong box is removed or corrected\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-5.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\